The rotation is the standard 90-degree clockwise rule: row i, column j of the original becomes row j, column n - 1 - i of the output, where n is the original number of rows. That rule is followed by taking each input column and building a row from it while reading the original rows backwards. The outer loop ranges over columns, including the full range len(grid[0]) so that an input with missing trailing rows still gets counted as being rectangular, and the inner comprehension reverses the row indices to preserve that ordering.

